@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch13ch14-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch13ch14-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 13 and 14"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch13ch14-lineage/1.0.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch13ch14_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment "1.0.0 (2026-11-10): Mission stage. Opened as its own narrow lineage, same pattern as Lineage3 (ch09ch10) and Lineage4 (ch11ch12), per the owner's standing rule to prefer simple, narrow, closeable lineages over one broad package-wide lineage, and confirmed again this turn ('plan chapters 13-14'). ORDINAL FINDING, checked against the live register before this was opened (lineage-practice-lessons.md: ordinals/IDs are taken from the live register's own next-free number, never assigned informally): the slides-lineage register (sen0414_slides_lineage_v2_402_0.ttl) already holds its own ex:Lineage3 (ordinal 3, exam work, LS_Abandoned) and ex:Lineage4 (ordinal 4, two-exams mission, LS_InProgress) - unrelated to, and in a different IRI namespace from, this session's ch09ch10 lineage (independently named Lineage3/ordinal 3 in its own file) and ch11ch12 lineage (independently named Lineage4/ordinal 4 in its own file). No technical/data collision (distinct IRIs), but the ordinal sequence was not actually unique package-wide as the convention intends; this happened because the two chapter-pair lineages were opened without checking the slides register's own ordinals first. Owner's ruling (asked, since it rests on no prior stated rule): note it here, leave ex:Lineage3 (ch09ch10) and ex:Lineage4 (ch11ch12) as the historical record unedited, and number forward from the true next-free ordinal across all lineage files found this turn, which is 5. This lineage therefore takes ordinal 5."@en .

## --- Profile declaration (ceremony step 1) ---

ex:ProfileDecl5 a backlog:ProfileDeclaration ;
    rdfs:label "Profile: AAL (agentic adaptive), default"@en ;
    backlog:declaresProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:declaresLevel backlog:Level_L2 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Default ;
    backlog:hasDeclarationRationale "Same declaration as Lineage3 and Lineage4 (ex:ProfileDecl, ex:ProfileDecl4): work is executed by an LLM agent, no human team; AAL is the default profile for agent-executed work and this lineage names none other. Level L2 stated plainly because this lineage does not re-run the full SHACL/register tooling used by the BRSF framework's own self-governance against this course repository's simplified lineage files." ;
    backlog:declaredAt "2026-11-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:reviewDate "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date .

## --- Lineage ---

ex:Lineage5 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 13 and 14, narrow lineage"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission5 ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 5 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Opened ;
    backlog:hasProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:followsProfileDeclaration ex:ProfileDecl5 ;
    backlog:continuesFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    rdfs:comment "ex:Lineage2 (sen0414-slides-lineage namespace) is the closed SEN0414 slides lineage this continues from, same as Lineage3 and Lineage4 before it. Chapters 13 and 14's structural retrofit (TK_Ret_Ch13_*, TK_Ret_Ch14_*) was recorded Done in that closed lineage before it closed, so no open item is carried forward; this lineage opens fresh on a mission the owner is stating now, parallel to, not continuing, Lineage3 or Lineage4."@en .

## --- Mission ---

ex:Mission5 a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 13 and 14 taught from one approved draft each"@en ;
    backlog:missionFor ex:Backlog5 ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "Chapters 13 (Web Scraping) and 14 (Excel Spreadsheets) of the third edition are taught with a deck and an interactive page, each produced from one owner-approved chapter draft, following the same review given to chapters 9-10 and 11-12: a true, sourced, pedagogically-motivated story per concept the chapter actually teaches (per the owner's 2026-11-09 principle - story count is not preset, but important history of the concepts must be covered within time and scope), an accurate resources slide, and any open items named and closed before build." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin "Owner's instruction this conversation, 2026-11-10 ('Fine proceed' confirming 'plan chapters 13-14'), following the Lineage3/Lineage4 pattern and their own stated exclusion that later chapter pairs get their own narrow lineages, rather than widening either mission." .

## --- Scope (taxonomic: areas, deliverables, exclusions - G194) ---

ex:Scope5 a backlog:ScopeStatement ;
    rdfs:label "Draft, check and (on approval) render chapters 13-14 only"@en ;
    backlog:scopeForMission ex:Mission5 ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:scopeCompletionState backlog:Proposed ;
    backlog:coversArea ex:Area5_StateCheck, ex:Area5_Draft, ex:Area5_Render ;
    backlog:hasScopeExclusion ex:Excl5_Ch1to12, ex:Excl5_OtherChapters, ex:Excl5_ExamWork, ex:Excl5_RenderBeforeApproval, ex:Excl5_StructuralRetrofit ;
    backlog:hasScopeDeliverable ex:Del5_ApprovedDraft, ex:Del5_CheckedMaterials ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "IN: for chapters 13 (Web Scraping: HTTP/HTTPS, downloading files with the requests module, a weather API, parsing HTML, Beautiful Soup, browser automation with Selenium and with Playwright) and 14 (Excel Spreadsheets: reading and writing .xlsx files with openpyxl, setting font style, formulas, adjusting rows and columns, charts) of the 3rd edition only - (a) read the existing deck, page, research/ABox, the two chapters' already-self-checked story-companion scripts (sen0414_ch13_stories_v1_0_1.py, sen0414_ch14_stories_v1_0_0.py) and say plainly what is stale, missing, or duplicated against the owner's 2026-11-09 story principle and current resources-slide standard; (b) write one plain-text chapter draft per chapter (story per 5N1K using the real, already-sourced companion-script beats, explanations, slide outline, page-tab outline in slide order, each non-network code example with its executed result and each network/browser example checked for syntax and documented-library correctness, resources slide) for the owner's reading and approval; (c) ONLY after approval, render the deck, page and document from that one draft, versioned per the 2026-11-08 version rule (each file its own step, sized to the change). OUT: chapters 1-12 (chapters 1-8 midterm scope untouched; chapters 9-10 are Lineage3's own mission, 11-12 are Lineage4's own mission, neither widened here); chapters 15 and onward (later narrow lineages, same pattern); exam and mock-exam work (held outside this repository); rendering before the owner's approval of the draft; the structural chapter-check/retrofit against the iteration-20 standard (TK_Ret_Ch13_*, TK_Ret_Ch14_*), already Done in the closed Lineage2 and not reopened without a found defect." .

ex:Area5_StateCheck a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "What exists for chapters 13-14 today"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 .
ex:Area5_Draft a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "The one approved draft per chapter"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 .
ex:Area5_Render a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Deck, page and document rendered from the approved draft"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 .

ex:Del5_ApprovedDraft a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Owner-approved plain-text draft, chapters 13 and 14"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area5_Draft .
ex:Del5_CheckedMaterials a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Chapter-13/14 materials checked against current standard, gaps named"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area5_StateCheck .

ex:Excl5_Ch1to12 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Chapters 1-12"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Chapters 1-8 are midterm scope, untouched; chapters 9-10 are Lineage3's own live/closed mission and 11-12 are Lineage4's own closed mission, neither widened by this lineage." .
ex:Excl5_OtherChapters a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Chapters 15-25"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Later chapter pairs get their own narrow lineages, same pattern as this one, Lineage3 and Lineage4." .
ex:Excl5_ExamWork a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Exam and mock-exam work"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Held outside this repository." .
ex:Excl5_RenderBeforeApproval a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Rendering a deck/page/document before the draft is approved"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Same draft-first rule applied in Lineage3 and Lineage4: layout built before content is settled was the measured cause of the five-build-per-page slowness." .
ex:Excl5_StructuralRetrofit a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "The iteration-20 structural chapter-check/retrofit for chapters 13-14"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Already recorded Done in the closed Lineage2 (TK_Ret_Ch13_*, TK_Ret_Ch14_*). Reopening it without a found defect would be re-litigating a closed finding; this lineage's state-check (Area5_StateCheck) is the narrower, pedagogical-story-and-resources check only." .
